1
00:00:00,730 --> 00:00:01,970
(Sheldon:)Uh, for regular readers

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:04,470
of The New England Journal
of High Energy Physics,

3
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:05,940
(Sheldon:)I need no introduction.

4
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,340
(Sheldon:)If you're not familiar

5
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:08,620
(Sheldon:)with that publication,

6
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:11,280
(Sheldon:)there's a free copy
in your goody bag.

7
00:00:13,110 --> 00:00:15,160
(Sheldon:)Stuart?

8
00:00:16,020 --> 00:00:18,280
Um... (clears throat) Hi.

9
00:00:18,280 --> 00:00:19,550
(Stuart:)I'm Stuart.

10
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:21,350
(Stuart:)I run a comic bookstore,

11
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:25,320
(Stuart:)which for financial reasons,
I'm currently living in.

12
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,090
(Stuart:)And I guess

13
00:00:27,090 --> 00:00:30,560
(Stuart:)what I'm hoping for most out
of tonight is a hot shower.

14
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,430
It's very
nice, Stuart.

15
00:00:32,430 --> 00:00:34,180
(Sheldon:)Zack?

16
00:00:34,180 --> 00:00:36,300
(Zack:)I'm Zack, and I'm, uh...

17
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,600
(Howard:)Uh...

18
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:42,910
(Zack:)Could you come back to me?

19
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:44,530
(Leonard:)Of course.

20
00:00:44,530 --> 00:00:46,510
(Sheldon:)Barry?

21
00:00:46,510 --> 00:00:47,680
(Barry:)I'm Barry Kwipke, and I'm here

22
00:00:47,680 --> 00:00:50,250
(Barry:)because you told me
there was going to be a whaffle.

23
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:53,890
(Barry:)When is the whaffle?

24
00:00:53,890 --> 00:00:55,350
(Sheldon:)Patience, patience, Barry.

25
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:56,540
The whaffle... (clears throat)

26
00:00:56,540 --> 00:00:59,790
The raffle is the grand finale

27
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:03,500
(Sheldon:)to an evening-long festival
of fun and folly.

